; board-view.sabra — the windowed board read (board.borg L6).
;
; Inputs: the granted prefix ("todo/", WITH the slash - collation
; excludes sibling probe namespaces) and the cursor (EXCLUSIVE lower
; bound, "" = first window).  Window size 24 keeps a window of
; real-sized records (cstr titles are bit-lists: ~2KB ternary per
; entry) inside the journal payload cap; the payloads' loud caps are
; the protection, never a silent truncation.
;
; Result: (pair <window entries> <summary>) where the entries are the
; tree/list answer verbatim (path, value, version each) and the
; summary is the dialect 12.4 keyed record: key 1 = open count,
; key 2 = done count - per-window counts only, recorded so they
; cannot masquerade as totals.
;
; The count folds use the todo-open-count idiom verbatim (math/add
; fires EVERY element, so a denied prim denies the count, never
; silently - the 0014 law); let-aliasing does not re-fire the prim
; (probe-pinned: one tree/list row per window however many refs).
; tree-eq is pure; no other prims ride this read.

(lambda (pfx)
  (lambda (cursor)
    (let ((items (prim "tree/list" pfx cursor "24")))
      (let ((opens (todo-open-count items)))
        (pair items
          (pair
            (pair key-state (pair opens %0))
            (pair (pair key-title (pair
              (list-fold
                (lambda (e) (lambda (acc)
                  (if (prim "math/add" acc 1) acc
                    (tree-eq (todo-state (todo-entry e)) todo-done))))
                0 items)
              %0)) %0)))))))
